## PART 1 — THE MINDSET SHIFT

Most builders think "good UI" means pretty colors and nice fonts. That's maybe 15% of what makes something feel premium. The other 85% is invisible until it's missing.

**Top-tier products feel "expensive" because of three things:**

1. **Restraint** — they do less, but everything they do is perfect. Linear doesn't have 40 features on the dashboard. It has 6, and each one is flawless.
2. **Consistency at the microscopic level** — every button, every spacing, every transition follows the same rules. Nothing is "close enough."
3. **Anticipation of the user** — the product reacts before you realize you needed it to. Loading states, hover hints, smart defaults, empty states that teach you what to do next.

The goal isn't "more features." The goal is "every interaction feels considered."

